    {
      "id": 69056,
      "name": "jagarciao",
      "username": "jagarciao",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/jagarciao/{size}/2010_2.png",
      "created_at": "2013-08-01T22:16:16.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>But it would also be logical and within reason to have the H reduced since H is defined in the rules as the \"current\" number of players... but we have been told that H is, in fact, not reduced when a player leaves the game for some reason.&nbsp;</p><p>So, while logic is indeed on your side, we can't really rely on logic to dictate rulings anymore.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I have to admit that all this ambiguous wordings and sometimes counterintuitive or even contradictory situations has been taking away from the game a little bit for me. I do love the game and have a group of people I play with where we don't have a problem because we have such a laid attitude about how things work and we tweak them freely as necessary... but I have often had a hard time explaining (or defending) certain card interactions when trying to bring the game to new players... to the point that I tend to avoid it and just stick to playing with my group only.&nbsp;</p>",
      "post_number": 12,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:47:32.358Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
