      "can_see_hidden_post": false,
      "can_wiki": false,
      "read": false,
      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "<p>But it would also be logical and within reason to have the H reduced since H is defined in the rules as the &quot;current&quot; number of players... but we have been told that H is, in fact, not reduced when a player leaves the game for some reason.&nbsp;</p><p>So, while logic is indeed on your side, we can&#39;t really rely on logic to dictate rulings anymore.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I have to admit that all this ambiguous wordings and sometimes counterintuitive or even contradictory situations has been taking away from the game a little bit for me. I do love the game and have a group of people I play with where we don&#39;t have a problem because we have such a laid attitude about how things work and we tweak them freely as necessary... but I have often had a hard time explaining (or defending) certain card interactions when trying to bring the game to new players... to the point that I tend to avoid it and just stick to playing with my group only.&nbsp;</p>",
