      "raw": "[quote=\"jagarciao\"]\n\nBut it would also be logical and within reason to have the H reduced since H is defined in the rules as the &quot;current&quot; number of players... but we have been told that H is, in fact, not reduced when a player leaves the game for some reason.&nbsp;So, while logic is indeed on your side, we can&#39;t really rely on logic to dictate rulings anymore.&nbsp;&nbsp;I have to admit that all this ambiguous wordings and sometimes counterintuitive or even contradictory situations has been taking away from the game a little bit for me. I do love the game and have a group of people I play with where we don&#39;t have a problem because we have such a laid attitude about how things work and we tweak them freely as necessary... but I have often had a hard time explaining (or defending) certain card interactions when trying to bring the game to new players... to the point that I tend to avoid it and just stick to playing with my group only.&nbsp;\n\n[/quote]\n\nYeah I understand that totally. Just the other day I was playing with a few new people to the game and took slight issue with one of the interactions (I don&#39;t remember which), but made a pretty decent thematic argument for it so I allowed it. At the end of day, you still just gotta have fun with it.&nbsp;\n",
